# Gifted and Talented Youth as Philosophers of the New Millennium.

**Authors:** McGregor, Gerald D., Jr.

## Abstract
This article proposes that teaching gifted students elegant problem solving in the arts and sciences requires curriculum that includes philosophical inquiry. Discussion focuses on a rationale for philosophical inquiry, philosophy within the humanities, philosophy as curriculum, and the need for theoretical models that are easily understood and used by teachers. (Contains references.) (DB)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ624857

